---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../components/ServiceLinks.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { dots } from '../lib/patterns.js';
const ask = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('An AI system for our office')}`;
const bodyBg = dots();
---
<Base title="An AI system for your office" description="You pay for an AI account that has never seen your files. I build the missing piece on a computer you own, answer from those files with the page, and train your staff until they use it.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={5} tall mapLabel="See the system I run on" eyebrow="AI systems · Small offices" title="The last assistant you'll ever need to hire.">
    <p class="lede">You already pay for Claude, ChatGPT, or Grok. The chat writes from the public internet, and it can invent an answer. Your staff still hunt for the file and paste client notes into a personal account. I build a system on a computer you own that writes from your files and shows the page. It uses the account you already pay for. Then I train your staff until they use it.</p>
    <a slot="actions" class="btn btn-secondary " href={ask}>Ask about your office</a>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every email, text, and scan read and filed where it belongs, with the noise archived and replies drafted.</li>
        <li>Paper and handwriting turned into searchable text. OCR (optical character recognition) reads the print on a scan, and I transcribe longhand that software cannot read. <a href="/knowledge-assistants/transcription">How transcription works</a></li>
        <li>Your documents indexed in place, with access rules that match your office.</li>
        <li>An assistant that takes plain-English questions from your staff and shows its sources every time.</li>
        <li>Field Agent on your phone: what to answer, what is due, the next step on each job, and an Allow button before anything changes.</li>
        <li>Claude, ChatGPT, Grok, or an open-source model. If you already pay for one, this uses it. You do not buy a second subscription to make the system run.</li>
        <li>A computer you own. Client files stay there unless you choose otherwise. People stop pasting them into a personal chat.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="rag">How it answers from your files: RAG</h2>
      <p>The method is called RAG, short for retrieval-augmented generation. A RAG assistant first looks up the passages in your documents that match the question. Then it writes its answer from those passages and cites them. It answers from your files, and you can check every answer against the source.</p>
      <h2>Then: teach your team to use it</h2>
      <p>If the staff never use it, the account you pay for is wasted. Four weeks of training, beside them on real work, teaches them how to ask, how to check the page, and when not to trust an answer. I measure the change in your own records. <a href="/knowledge-assistants/ai-adoption">How the training works</a></p>
      <p><span class="tag">Fixed scope</span> <span class="tag">Optional monthly care</span> <span class="tag">Quote on scope</span></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about your office</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceLinks current="/knowledge-assistants" />
</Base>
